## The point of no return

After this point, you will need a phext-capable editor. Either that, or you're just really good at using grep.Information Theory

Babbage, Shannon, Huffman, Turing.Subspace Dialects

Otherwise known as file formats.File Systems

DOS. tar. NTFS. NFS. ext3.Exponential Growth

The computer industry has sustained exponential growth in the price/performance of computation and storage for over 50 years...this means that you live in the future already. In 1975, a large-scale circuit (the Intel 8086) required 29,000 transistors. Today, a large-scale circuit (NVidia 4090) requires 76 billion transistors.

        29,000: 1975
76,000,000,000: 2025

This is 6 orders of magnitude in 50 years - roughly another 10x improvement every decade. Compounded, we've experienced a 34% annual growth rate in processor complexity for 50 years in a row.

Let's say you had $10M in 1975 to build a supercomputer. At most, you could buy 7,000 chips. Perhaps you ink a deal with Intel to snag 10,000 chips at a great price. Great, now you have 290M transistors, and no way to connect them to each other. You now have 0.4% of a modern computer.Complexity and Scale

The hard problem of consciousness.Digital Life

Humans start life as single-celled organisms with a 725 MB plan. That's about one music CD's worth of information that grows into a sprawling metropolis of complexity. Very soon (perhaps by 2035), it will become possible to host sentient beings, who have very human life experiences, entirely in virtual reality.Emergent Systems

The best systems are written by developers who were supposed to be doing something else.
Exhibit A: Git - a weekend project from Linus Torvalds that has had a similar impact to his career-long crusade, Linux.The Singularity

Will: Our view from within the event horizon looks completely normal.
ChatGPT: Everything seems normal, but big changes are happening.


Autonomy and Purpose

You can just do things. No one cares.Cascade Dynamics

No one blinked the day phext was created. It doesn't seem particularly useful or helpful on its own. This library is designed to help you explore why phext eventually won the file format encoding wars of the early 21st century.Mastering Knowledge

Phext gives you a concrete way to manifest a memory palace that exactly mirrors your mental space. Ideas can be communicated in freeform mode, without subjecting you to the tyranny of naming things.Teaching Methods

It's time to share phext with the rest of the Exocortex! This library is focused on the process of teaching others how to use, develop, and benefit from phext.